<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Sorting Polynomials by Factoring Methods</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01686</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Sorting Polynomials by Factoring Methods</md:title>
    <md:uuid>031624f3-68e2-4c28-873c-2a915ccaaac0</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Cool Down</title>

      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00001">Examine the following polynomials:<newline/>
<m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>27</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>q</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math><newline/>
<m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>25</m:mn><m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math><newline/>
<m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo><m:mn>72</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>81</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math><newline/>
<m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>36</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math><newline/>
<m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>p</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo><m:mn>100</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math><newline/>
<m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>36</m:mn> <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo> <m:msup><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para>

          <para id="sortpoly">Sort the polynomials by whether you would factor them using the difference of squares or the perfect square trinomial method.</para>
          <para id="para-00002">Draw a table similar to this on a sheet of paper. Record your results. If a polynomial requires both methods, place it in both columns.</para>
          <table class="unnumbered os-raise-midsizetable" id="table-00001">
            <tgroup cols="2">
              <thead><row>
                  <entry>
                    <emphasis>Difference of Squares Method</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <emphasis>Perfect Square Trinomial Method</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                </thead><tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                    <newline/>
                    <newline/>
                    <newline/>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <newline/>
                    <newline/>
                    <newline/>
                  </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </tgroup>
          </table>
          <para id="para-00003"/>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">Compare your answers:</para>
          <table class="unnumbered os-raise-midsizetable" id="table-00002">
            <tgroup cols="2">
              <thead><row>
                  <entry>
                    <emphasis>Difference of Squares Method</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <emphasis>Perfect Square Trinomial Method</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                </thead><tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry><para id="para-00007">
                    <m:math display="inline">
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>27</m:mn>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>q</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                        <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:math></para><para id="para-00008">
          <m:math display="inline">
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                        <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>100</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:math></para><para id="para-00009">
          <m:math display="inline">
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                        <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>10</m:mn>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                        <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>25</m:mn>
                        <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:math></para><para id="para-00010">
          <m:math display="inline">
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                        <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>12</m:mn>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                        <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>36</m:mn>
                        <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:math></para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry><para id="para-00011">
                    <m:math display="inline">
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>16</m:mn>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                        <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>72</m:mn>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                        <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>81</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:math></para><para id="para-00012">
          <m:math display="inline">
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>36</m:mn>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                        <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>12</m:mn>
                        <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                        <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:math></para><para id="para-00013">
          <m:math display="inline">
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                        <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>10</m:mn>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                        <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>25</m:mn>
                        <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:math></para><para id="para-00014">
          <m:math display="inline">
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                        <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>12</m:mn>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                        <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                        <m:mn>36</m:mn>
                        <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                        <m:msup>
                          <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                          <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                        </m:msup>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:math></para>
                  </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </tgroup>
          </table>
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <note id="note-00001">
        <title>Why Should I Care?</title>
          <media alt="Illustration of a woman wearing an orange apron arranging a bouquet of flowers at a table, surrounded by vases, flower arrangements, scissors, and string, with a floral picture on the wall behind her.">
          <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_07_09_09_01.png" width="200"/>
        </media>
        
        <para id="para-00005">Ozzie Gomez and Juan Casava own a store called Plant Shop Chicago. They use polynomials everyday to make sure the operations of their small business go smoothly.</para>
        <para id="para-00006">One of the most important parts of running a business is understanding where your money is going. You need to know how much you are spending and how much you are making. For example, Ozzie Gomez and Juan Cassava can use polynomials to calculate how many different plants they can buy and how much money they can make off of each sale.</para>
      </note>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>